WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.530
In 1909, Carl Correns crossed
four-o'clock plants with green,

2
00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.800
white and patchy leaves.

3
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:10.510
The seedlings always matched the
branch that supplied the ovule.

4
00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.550
The pollen's branch made
no difference at all.

5
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.010
So how can some traits pass from
mothers to all their children,

6
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.250
but not from fathers?

7
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.740
In this mission, you'll meet a single
gene that affects the skeleton,

8
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:25.000
the eyes and the heart.

9
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:29.650
Then you'll design crosses that
reveal which parent passes a trait on.

10
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:34.350
Your mission: explain how some traits
pass from mothers to all their children,

11
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.130
but not from fathers.
